[{:db/id "30a55d4b-f895-53a5-a364-ce5fddbb6ae1" :answer/id #uuid "30a55d4b-f895-53a5-a364-ce5fddbb6ae1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "028288df-333f-57f2-9e25-7548b283399c" :answer/id #uuid "028288df-333f-57f2-9e25-7548b283399c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cb3d8d25-8bfa-5e2a-b032-69c3782c0eb7" :answer/id #uuid "cb3d8d25-8bfa-5e2a-b032-69c3782c0eb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(25,0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "66291432-b739-52c2-992c-c3d5906e8d52" :answer/id #uuid "66291432-b739-52c2-992c-c3d5906e8d52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(376,0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "59d2a5db-49a2-566c-afa9-b7bdaafa25da" :answer/id #uuid "59d2a5db-49a2-566c-afa9-b7bdaafa25da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{376}{25},0)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "40ab1d54-64ea-58e4-9d91-d527f34b3bee" :answer-field/id #uuid "40ab1d54-64ea-58e4-9d91-d527f34b3bee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["30a55d4b-f895-53a5-a364-ce5fddbb6ae1" "028288df-333f-57f2-9e25-7548b283399c" "cb3d8d25-8bfa-5e2a-b032-69c3782c0eb7" "66291432-b739-52c2-992c-c3d5906e8d52" "59d2a5db-49a2-566c-afa9-b7bdaafa25da"] :answer-field/correct "66291432-b739-52c2-992c-c3d5906e8d52" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" :question/id #uuid "7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x)=10 x^{2} + 5 x$ at the point $(1,15)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 x^{2} + 5 x)=20 x + 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=25=25,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(25)}=- \\frac{1}{25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(15)&=- \\frac{1}{25}(x-(1))\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x-(- \\frac{1}{25})+(15)\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}&=0\\\\x&=376.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(376,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["40ab1d54-64ea-58e4-9d91-d527f34b3bee"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "93fb4c05-1e1a-5463-aeeb-5bdc06ba8f62" :answer/id #uuid "93fb4c05-1e1a-5463-aeeb-5bdc06ba8f62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1080" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7468eab7-aa1d-581c-b1c7-75e4eb6144f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "7468eab7-aa1d-581c-b1c7-75e4eb6144f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["93fb4c05-1e1a-5463-aeeb-5bdc06ba8f62"] :answer-field/correct "93fb4c05-1e1a-5463-aeeb-5bdc06ba8f62" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "17fbaf02-25c3-5f36-8455-1d21e7ade415" :answer/id #uuid "17fbaf02-25c3-5f36-8455-1d21e7ade415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f7f48b25-30b8-5af5-8b60-15f91577b14d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7f48b25-30b8-5af5-8b60-15f91577b14d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["17fbaf02-25c3-5f36-8455-1d21e7ade415"] :answer-field/correct "17fbaf02-25c3-5f36-8455-1d21e7ade415" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" :question/id #uuid "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30$ at the point $(0,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30)=36 x - 36.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(0)=-36=-36,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-36)}=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{36}(x-(0))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{36}x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x+30&=0\\\\\\frac{1}{36}x&=-30\\\\x&=-1080.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(-1080,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["7468eab7-aa1d-581c-b1c7-75e4eb6144f4" "f7f48b25-30b8-5af5-8b60-15f91577b14d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "4079920d-ee6c-5086-9aa8-97eb49b915c2" :answer/id #uuid "4079920d-ee6c-5086-9aa8-97eb49b915c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-599" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "24d2eda6-5f52-58d1-8821-c19db30c5bf9" :answer-field/id #uuid "24d2eda6-5f52-58d1-8821-c19db30c5bf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["4079920d-ee6c-5086-9aa8-97eb49b915c2"] :answer-field/correct "4079920d-ee6c-5086-9aa8-97eb49b915c2" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "ba9c2120-ea78-56ae-b7da-fc8f913f4ff6" :answer/id #uuid "ba9c2120-ea78-56ae-b7da-fc8f913f4ff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a11eaf98-7e1d-530f-93f1-50c6c3aa85a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "a11eaf98-7e1d-530f-93f1-50c6c3aa85a7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["ba9c2120-ea78-56ae-b7da-fc8f913f4ff6"] :answer-field/correct "ba9c2120-ea78-56ae-b7da-fc8f913f4ff6" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286" :question/id #uuid "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{20}{x}+10$ at the point $(1,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{20}{x}+10)\\\\&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 + \\frac{20}{x})\\\\&=-20x^{-2}\\\\&=- \\frac{20}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=-20=-20,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-20)}=\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{20}(x-(1))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x-(\\frac{1}{20})+(30)\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}&=0\\\\x&=-599.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(-599,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["24d2eda6-5f52-58d1-8821-c19db30c5bf9" "a11eaf98-7e1d-530f-93f1-50c6c3aa85a7"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "6f93f05c-93ce-5432-b4e0-7ec958ee8e90" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186092385.py"} [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions ["7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286"]} [:db/ensure 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/validate]]
